  "note": "Triennial election of Lisburn Urban District Council, polled on Tuesday 15 January 1929 in the North and Central Wards. In the South Ward (4 seats) five were nominated and John F. Floyd withdrew, so there was no contest. Four seats; five nominated, John F. Floyd withdrew: no contest (LS 11 Jan 1929 p8, nominations a151 and withdrawals a152). Returned unopposed."
